Description: Slides: the window and the presenter view of the Wild OS presentation app
 Impress dressed as Slides, beside Write and Tables.
 .
 The status bar reads as on the Slides board: the slide and how many there
 are, the name of the slide's layout (in place of its master's, which is
 "Default" for nearly every slide; in English the short Wild OS names), the
 language and the zoom.
 .
 At first start the sidebar is closed to its tab strip in Impress too, and
 the notes under the slide are a short strip instead of most of the window.
 .
 The presenter's own screen during a show can be arranged as on the Slides
 presenter board. It is switched on by configuration, by listing the
 Presenter/TopBar view in the presenter layout, which wildos-slides.xcd in
 the wildos-slides package does; without it LibreOffice's own arrangement is
 untouched. With it: a top bar with the file name, "Slide 2 of 6", a timer
 (04:12) and the clock (10:24); the slide on screen large on the left, the
 next slide and the notes on the right, each under a small label; and along
 the bottom pill buttons, the slide sorter as a one-row strip of thumbnails
 that follows the show, and End show. New for it are tool bar entries drawn
 as pills (Name starting with Pill), labels for the file name and slide
 count, a right anchor for a bar, three more tool bar views (TopBar, TimeBar,
 EndBar) and the UsePointer, UsePen and BlackScreen actions. The notes lose
 their zoom buttons and Close, and previews their transition markers.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

